1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,357
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:03,001
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,521 --> 00:00:05,389
(Episode 40)

4
00:00:11,981 --> 00:00:13,942
Hey.

5
00:00:14,875 --> 00:00:16,806
You still haven't gone to work?

6
00:00:17,966 --> 00:00:20,101
Mai is coming. I'll see her before I go.

7
00:00:20,193 --> 00:00:23,519
How can you be so irresponsible
about your job?

8
00:00:23,654 --> 00:00:24,676
Come on, go.

9
00:00:24,741 --> 00:00:27,451
What happens in this house stays here.
You take care of your own work. Go on.

10
00:00:29,592 --> 00:00:30,823
Didn't you hear me?

11
00:00:32,778 --> 00:00:34,187
I quit. I'm unemployed.

12
00:00:34,457 --> 00:00:36,347
What? Why?

13
00:00:36,547 --> 00:00:38,625
You were doing all that work
at the publishing company. Why quit?

14
00:00:38,627 --> 00:00:41,006
It was too much. That job wasn't for me.

15
00:00:41,538 --> 00:00:44,118
- I might just get a part-time job.
- A part-time job?

16
00:00:44,172 --> 00:00:45,966
Listen to you.

17
00:00:46,032 --> 00:00:47,950
Do you know how hard part-time jobs are?

18
00:00:48,453 --> 00:00:50,652
How would you know? You've never had one.

19
00:00:50,698 --> 00:00:52,199
You've played the cello your whole life.

20
00:00:52,202 --> 00:00:55,085
Well, anyway...

21
00:00:55,392 --> 00:00:57,072
What really happened?

22
00:00:57,115 --> 00:01:00,150
Why did you suddenly quit?
Did they fire you?

23
00:01:00,912 --> 00:01:02,896
They worked you to the bone,
then decided they didn't need you?

24
00:01:02,943 --> 00:01:04,604
Yeah. They said they didn't.

25
00:01:06,185 --> 00:01:10,025
No, it's not that.
I just need some time off. Is that okay?

26
00:01:10,303 --> 00:01:12,593
Just support me for a while, Mom.

27
00:01:13,696 --> 00:01:14,997
What about your things?

28
00:01:15,065 --> 00:01:16,878
I'll bring them back little by little.

29
00:01:17,651 --> 00:01:19,942
Go change. I'll come with you.

30
00:01:20,728 --> 00:01:22,712
Forget it. Since when do you do that?

31
00:01:22,715 --> 00:01:23,962
That's right.

32
00:01:24,088 --> 00:01:27,850
I never once came to your school.
Let me do this much for you now.

33
00:01:28,265 --> 00:01:29,984
You have a lot of stuff. Come on.

34
00:01:40,172 --> 00:01:41,172
Mai.

35
00:01:43,832 --> 00:01:45,512
I'm sorry I startled you.

36
00:02:11,396 --> 00:02:13,073
I thought you'd be making seaweed soup.

37
00:02:14,677 --> 00:02:16,359
Yeah. Thanks.

38
00:02:18,732 --> 00:02:19,937
How is she?

39
00:02:20,564 --> 00:02:21,786
She's hanging in there.

40
00:02:24,178 --> 00:02:28,318
She came all the way to a foreign country
and now she's going through all this.

41
00:02:31,867 --> 00:02:32,867
Are you crying?

42
00:02:33,212 --> 00:02:37,637
Yeah. It's sad. She's such a good kid.

43
00:02:39,355 --> 00:02:43,923
- This year has been so hard.
- I know.

44
00:02:47,763 --> 00:02:50,507
If you're going to cry,
go cry in your room.

45
00:02:50,968 --> 00:02:52,290
Aren't you sad?

46
00:02:53,605 --> 00:02:54,670
No, I'm not.

47
00:02:56,618 --> 00:02:58,484
You're really strong.

48
00:03:02,392 --> 00:03:06,484
Yeong Ju, Sa Bin's going to propose.

49
00:03:07,154 --> 00:03:08,969
Are you going to say yes?

50
00:03:09,670 --> 00:03:11,831
I heard you like Sa Bin too.

51
00:03:12,304 --> 00:03:14,404
You two really make a great couple.

52
00:03:15,130 --> 00:03:16,905
Do you really want to talk
about that right now?

53
00:03:17,263 --> 00:03:19,450
Keep quiet before the kids hear you,
and get on with what you're doing.

54
00:03:34,052 --> 00:03:35,635
Mai, I'm heading to work.

55
00:03:37,065 --> 00:03:40,232
Okay. Go.

56
00:03:40,644 --> 00:03:43,251
I'm fine, so don't worry about me.

57
00:03:45,725 --> 00:03:48,408
Why do you keep saying you're fine?
You're making me worry.

58
00:03:49,077 --> 00:03:50,789
I really am fine.

59
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,206
Eat lots of seaweed soup.

60
00:03:55,870 --> 00:03:57,338
Mom will be here.

61
00:03:58,752 --> 00:04:00,615
If anything happens,
make sure you call me.

62
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:05,284
See you tonight.

63
00:04:24,568 --> 00:04:25,568
Who is it?

64
00:04:26,907 --> 00:04:27,907
Mai.

65
00:04:28,104 --> 00:04:30,896
Are you okay? It must be really hard.

66
00:04:32,303 --> 00:04:33,771
Seung Woo.

67
00:04:34,350 --> 00:04:37,284
Don't make me laugh.
Did you practice that?

68
00:04:38,759 --> 00:04:41,633
Last time, you were the only one
speaking Korean,

69
00:04:42,398 --> 00:04:46,305
and I couldn't stop thinking about how you
said our family wasn't making any effort.

70
00:04:47,712 --> 00:04:49,092
I couldn't even say a word.

71
00:04:49,689 --> 00:04:54,230
I only said that because I was so angry
and wasn't thinking straight.

72
00:04:54,976 --> 00:04:56,201
Don't worry about it.

73
00:04:57,456 --> 00:04:59,535
I'm the one who came to Korea to study.

74
00:05:01,992 --> 00:05:05,398
I don't know how to comfort you
at a time like this,

75
00:05:06,114 --> 00:05:07,660
but an accident is just an accident.

76
00:05:08,052 --> 00:05:10,063
It wasn't your fault.
You know that, right?

77
00:05:11,082 --> 00:05:12,751
Did you feel that way too?

78
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:18,907
I tried to think that way.
I shouldn't have run that day.

79
00:05:19,390 --> 00:05:20,703
I should've just stayed put.

80
00:05:21,010 --> 00:05:22,421
I should've listened to mom.

81
00:05:24,012 --> 00:05:28,146
I had a lot of regrets,
but I decided it was all fate.

82
00:05:29,305 --> 00:05:30,305
Fate?

83
00:05:30,406 --> 00:05:33,969
It wasn't anyone's fault,
so don't dwell on it.

84
00:05:34,543 --> 00:05:38,006
Our whole family loves you so much, Mai.
You know that, right?

85
00:05:38,164 --> 00:05:41,190
- Want me to say it in Vietnamese again?
- No, it's okay.

86
00:05:42,235 --> 00:05:44,637
Thank you. I'll stay strong.

87
00:05:48,623 --> 00:05:49,623
Answer it.

88
00:05:54,146 --> 00:05:55,429
Yes.

89
00:06:06,597 --> 00:06:09,641
Are you having the meeting
at a shared office?

90
00:06:11,515 --> 00:06:13,510
How can you hold a cast meeting there?

91
00:06:13,752 --> 00:06:15,229
Postpone the meeting for now.

92
00:06:15,877 --> 00:06:18,925
We need to find an office first. Yes.

93
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:25,304
- Are you looking for an office?
- Yeah.

94
00:06:25,632 --> 00:06:28,766
- Hold it at our office.
- "Our office?"

95
00:06:29,352 --> 00:06:31,570
No. What would we even do there?

96
00:06:31,608 --> 00:06:34,331
Why not? You've been there.
You know the place.

97
00:06:34,467 --> 00:06:36,834
It's clean, and there's plenty of parking.
What's the problem?

98
00:06:36,837 --> 00:06:38,720
It's just sitting empty. Why spend money?

99
00:06:38,829 --> 00:06:40,422
I don't know what the issue is,
but hold it there.

100
00:06:40,618 --> 00:06:44,685
- I don't want to go there.
- You're still hung up on it.

101
00:06:44,976 --> 00:06:47,654
The past is the past. It's just an office.
What's the big deal?

102
00:06:48,648 --> 00:06:51,264
You still haven't let go of the office?

103
00:06:51,275 --> 00:06:52,807
It won't sell.

104
00:06:52,810 --> 00:06:57,133
And honestly,
I want to bring it back to life.

105
00:06:57,136 --> 00:06:58,720
I don't want to bring it back to life.

106
00:07:00,698 --> 00:07:04,177
Don't get hung up on weird things.
Just use it. It's free.

107
00:07:05,073 --> 00:07:07,187
- Why are you so obsessed with it?
- It was my husband's place.

108
00:07:07,208 --> 00:07:08,564
You want to just throw it all away?

109
00:07:11,145 --> 00:07:13,782
You know Yeong Ju
is dating someone, right?

110
00:07:13,785 --> 00:07:15,464
Things move on.

111
00:07:15,511 --> 00:07:19,525
Don't be stubborn for no reason.
You know the passcode, right?

112
00:07:35,928 --> 00:07:37,292
Mother.

113
00:07:40,692 --> 00:07:43,266
Why are you here?
I heard you two broke up.

114
00:07:43,981 --> 00:07:45,872
No, that's not it. Ji Hu always...

115
00:07:51,503 --> 00:07:55,220
Did you really steal her work?

116
00:07:56,318 --> 00:07:59,368
Did you copy her drawings
and give them to your father-in-law?

117
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:02,918
No. Why would I? I can draw well too.

118
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,735
Then what was it doing in your house?

119
00:08:04,825 --> 00:08:06,037
You stole it.

120
00:08:06,312 --> 00:08:09,966
They brought it there and lied,
saying I'd stolen it.

121
00:08:12,244 --> 00:08:15,862
Mother, even you don't believe me?

122
00:08:18,625 --> 00:08:21,074
Forget it. I don't care about that.

123
00:08:21,733 --> 00:08:23,007
That's my mother.

124
00:08:23,009 --> 00:08:27,110
My husband won't press the issue either,
so keep a low profile for now.

125
00:08:27,482 --> 00:08:29,473
- "Keep a low profile?"
- Just wait.

126
00:08:30,787 --> 00:08:34,177
A woman who clings to a man
morning and night...

127
00:08:35,023 --> 00:08:38,664
isn't very appealing. Besides, you know
how sensitive Ji Hu can be.

128
00:08:39,490 --> 00:08:41,752
He's not going to let this incident go.

129
00:08:41,755 --> 00:08:44,966
This is driving me crazy.
Why does something like that even matter?

130
00:08:45,585 --> 00:08:48,489
- Ji Hu is so frustrating.
- I find you even more frustrating.

131
00:08:48,492 --> 00:08:51,306
This is when you need to play hard to get.

132
00:08:51,550 --> 00:08:53,911
Don't come here, and don't contact him.

133
00:08:54,010 --> 00:08:56,597
But what if he really goes
to Ji Ni if I do that?

134
00:08:56,712 --> 00:08:59,457
Ji Ni? What is this, a magic lamp?

135
00:08:59,530 --> 00:09:04,160
Ji Hu has such high standards. You think
he'd fall for that mistress's daughter?

136
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:06,152
Don't be ridiculous.

137
00:09:06,310 --> 00:09:08,718
Just trust me
and play hard to get. Got it?

138
00:09:08,888 --> 00:09:10,791
You're going to be my daughter-in-law.

139
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:13,435
Are you sure I can really do that?

140
00:09:13,632 --> 00:09:15,643
Haven't you seen how I deal
with your father-in-law?

141
00:09:16,025 --> 00:09:17,978
The more desperate you are,
the more you need to play hard to get.

142
00:09:18,075 --> 00:09:21,662
A man you have to chase to keep
is a man who'll leave when you let go.

143
00:09:21,881 --> 00:09:24,591
- How can you live trusting such a man?
- Mother.

144
00:09:25,152 --> 00:09:28,271
I just can't do that.
My heart can't take it.

145
00:09:28,307 --> 00:09:31,183
Well, if you're so timid,
why did you cause such a mess?

146
00:09:31,573 --> 00:09:33,020
I understand.

147
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:43,286
I bought this for mom,
but she said she already had one.

148
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:46,614
I don't think you have anything
from this line, so I brought it for you.

149
00:09:54,235 --> 00:09:57,522
This is from the new line.

150
00:09:59,112 --> 00:10:02,952
But this isn't the time
to be giving gifts like this.

151
00:10:04,802 --> 00:10:09,233
Joong Bin's breakfast meeting ends soon.
He'll be back any minute.

152
00:10:09,601 --> 00:10:13,039
- See you at the publishing house.
- Okay.

153
00:10:30,682 --> 00:10:31,682
Yes.

154
00:10:36,391 --> 00:10:38,133
If this is about Do Hee,
let's talk later, Mom.

155
00:10:41,347 --> 00:10:44,637
You know you can't
break up with her, right?

156
00:10:46,046 --> 00:10:49,550
Do you think the Ambassador had no hand
in getting you promoted...

157
00:10:49,835 --> 00:10:52,282
- at the art center?
- Mom.

158
00:10:52,353 --> 00:10:54,367
Of course, you're talented.

159
00:10:54,370 --> 00:10:56,152
You are my son, after all.

160
00:10:57,065 --> 00:10:58,753
But honestly, is talent alone enough?

161
00:10:58,808 --> 00:11:01,227
Are you the only one
with your level of education and talent?

162
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:04,314
Getting ahead comes down to luck.

163
00:11:04,870 --> 00:11:09,204
And connections and money
create that luck. Don't they?

164
00:11:11,532 --> 00:11:13,408
Your dad and I can't give up on Do Hee.

165
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,755
You'd better understand that.

166
00:11:22,398 --> 00:11:24,575
Give Ji Ni a generous final payout.

167
00:11:24,585 --> 00:11:27,193
And find out who Sa Bin is seeing.

168
00:11:27,705 --> 00:11:29,646
But I don't have a description...

169
00:11:30,854 --> 00:11:31,854
Wait.

170
00:11:32,782 --> 00:11:34,877
Honey, show me that photo.

171
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:36,622
The woman you took
a picture of with Sa Bin.

172
00:11:38,530 --> 00:11:40,287
But you can't see her face.

173
00:11:46,811 --> 00:11:49,791
- I'll look into the people around him.
- Good.

174
00:11:57,473 --> 00:12:00,108
You need to keep an eye on Ji Hu.

175
00:12:00,798 --> 00:12:02,591
You heard they broke up, right?

176
00:12:03,646 --> 00:12:06,549
- Leave him alone for now.
- I told her he needs some time too.

177
00:12:06,552 --> 00:12:09,308
But Do Hee is really desperate.

178
00:12:09,912 --> 00:12:13,295
I'm worried the Ambassador
might hear about this.

179
00:12:15,799 --> 00:12:17,171
And...

180
00:12:17,587 --> 00:12:21,629
she keeps saying Ji Hu
is doing this because of Ji Ni.

181
00:12:22,291 --> 00:12:24,190
Are Ji Ni and Ji Hu close?

182
00:12:24,193 --> 00:12:25,535
Of course not. That's ridiculous.

183
00:12:25,690 --> 00:12:28,243
- It's because Ji Ni's close to Tae O.
- Right?

184
00:12:29,170 --> 00:12:33,202
Still, you never know,
so keep a close eye on him.

185
00:12:33,478 --> 00:12:34,493
I will.

186
00:12:36,366 --> 00:12:39,997
- What's that?
- Do Hee stopped by this morning.

187
00:12:40,450 --> 00:12:42,847
I sent her home and told her
to give him some time.

188
00:12:43,730 --> 00:12:46,892
- So that's what she brought.
- Return it.

189
00:12:47,232 --> 00:12:48,893
Who knows what people might say later?

190
00:12:52,269 --> 00:12:53,269
Do you want it?

191
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:58,509
- Because you won't buy me one.
- Then buy one.

192
00:12:58,572 --> 00:13:00,492
I'm giving you money.

193
00:13:00,938 --> 00:13:04,330
You always say what I buy is tacky,
so I don't buy anything. Buy it yourself.

194
00:13:04,395 --> 00:13:06,673
You'll faint when you hear the price.

195
00:13:06,753 --> 00:13:09,608
If it's expensive,
I'll just go back to sea.

196
00:13:10,197 --> 00:13:11,896
Honey.

197
00:13:11,936 --> 00:13:14,437
This is what makes life worth living.

198
00:13:15,035 --> 00:13:18,466
Who else am I doing this for?
Go ahead, spoil yourself.

199
00:13:32,517 --> 00:13:34,187
Are you still here?

200
00:13:38,765 --> 00:13:40,275
Can't you hear me?

201
00:13:41,835 --> 00:13:43,090
Was that you?

202
00:13:43,313 --> 00:13:44,850
I thought a dog was barking.

203
00:13:45,686 --> 00:13:46,997
Want to have one last round?

204
00:13:47,890 --> 00:13:49,281
Why are you provoking me again?

205
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:52,008
You're no match for me.

206
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:57,578
I have no interest in playing games.
Just focus on your art.

207
00:13:57,910 --> 00:14:00,268
I hope we meet at the top someday.

208
00:14:00,430 --> 00:14:02,926
- Not that I expect it.
- You little...

209
00:14:05,809 --> 00:14:09,327
How dare you hit my daughter
every chance you get?

210
00:14:09,810 --> 00:14:12,496
Stop following Ji Ni around.

211
00:14:12,538 --> 00:14:14,138
I'm sick and tired of it.

212
00:14:14,218 --> 00:14:16,118
Don't worry. It ends today.

213
00:14:16,570 --> 00:14:19,458
- She's getting kicked out, just like you.
- What?

214
00:14:19,572 --> 00:14:22,525
You got kicked out of the orchestra
and lost all your money.

215
00:14:22,816 --> 00:14:25,431
You've been mooching off his wife's
family, haven't you?

216
00:14:26,292 --> 00:14:28,845
You're just as shameless as I am.

217
00:14:29,598 --> 00:14:31,235
Or are you being punished?

218
00:14:31,566 --> 00:14:33,696
Punished for being a mistress?

219
00:14:33,785 --> 00:14:37,043
Watch your mouth, you little brat!

220
00:14:38,416 --> 00:14:39,737
Are you okay?

221
00:14:41,625 --> 00:14:44,366
Mom, she's the CEO's wife.

222
00:14:47,150 --> 00:14:49,812
- We've met before, right?
- Yes.

223
00:14:50,292 --> 00:14:52,896
I remember you being very rude.

224
00:14:55,111 --> 00:14:56,408
Rude?

225
00:14:57,507 --> 00:15:00,360
Could anything be ruder
than barging into someone's home?

226
00:15:01,212 --> 00:15:03,479
You clearly don't know what rude means.

227
00:15:04,138 --> 00:15:07,412
- She's your future daughter-in-law?
- Yes, she is.

228
00:15:08,472 --> 00:15:12,537
She has been suffering
because of your daughter.

229
00:15:13,149 --> 00:15:14,764
I'm sure she has.

230
00:15:15,898 --> 00:15:20,327
That talentless girl will do anything
to pretend she's talented,

231
00:15:20,450 --> 00:15:22,862
so we're both exhausted.

232
00:15:23,590 --> 00:15:24,854
I'm sure you are.

233
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:27,397
Now that society is more equal,

234
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:29,897
people who were never meant to mix
are forced to live together,

235
00:15:30,223 --> 00:15:32,597
- so we see things we'd rather not.
- What did you say?

236
00:15:32,652 --> 00:15:36,235
Just 100 years ago, I couldn't have spoken
to a mistress like this.

237
00:15:36,930 --> 00:15:41,118
I guess I was born a little too late,
so I'm forced to be this considerate.

238
00:15:41,953 --> 00:15:43,300
You're right, Mother.

239
00:15:43,330 --> 00:15:45,106
They're beneath us.

240
00:15:45,792 --> 00:15:47,564
Get your things out. Hurry.

241
00:15:47,658 --> 00:15:49,195
Mom, get out.

242
00:15:50,383 --> 00:15:53,403
Why don't you go back
100 years and live there?

243
00:15:59,284 --> 00:16:02,339
What are you doing?

244
00:16:03,962 --> 00:16:05,465
I guess there's no other choice.

245
00:16:05,541 --> 00:16:08,062
So much for your manners
when there's Coke around.

246
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:14,000
You little brat!

247
00:16:15,103 --> 00:16:16,757
This woman is seriously crazy...

248
00:16:16,810 --> 00:16:18,715
Mom. Get out.

249
00:16:23,932 --> 00:16:27,614
- How dare you...
- Mother, are you okay?

250
00:16:28,963 --> 00:16:30,243
Seriously!

251
00:16:31,869 --> 00:16:33,827
This is unbelievable!

252
00:16:59,952 --> 00:17:00,952
Mom.

253
00:17:02,950 --> 00:17:06,437
That's why I told you
you didn't have to come.

254
00:17:06,501 --> 00:17:07,904
If your dad were here,

255
00:17:07,992 --> 00:17:09,971
would he really let you
carry your own things?

256
00:17:10,058 --> 00:17:11,058
Mom.

257
00:17:11,781 --> 00:17:13,208
Succeed and get your revenge.

258
00:17:13,632 --> 00:17:16,729
Please marry someone even better
and make them regret it.

259
00:17:44,512 --> 00:17:47,335
What's wrong? Were you crying?

260
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:50,896
It's because of you.

261
00:17:51,190 --> 00:17:52,837
You think this is the first time
I've cried?

262
00:17:54,526 --> 00:17:55,882
It's all because of you.

263
00:17:55,936 --> 00:17:57,907
What are you talking about
all of a sudden?

264
00:17:57,910 --> 00:17:59,227
Do I look like I have it easy?

265
00:17:59,230 --> 00:18:01,877
- So you want to start a fight again?
- You should've dated sooner.

266
00:18:03,130 --> 00:18:06,760
- You should've remarried sooner.
- What are you even talking about?

267
00:18:07,061 --> 00:18:10,212
Ji Ni was bullied again today,

268
00:18:10,265 --> 00:18:14,171
because she's the daughter of a mistress.
Does she have to go through this?

269
00:18:14,352 --> 00:18:17,354
How long do I have to keep talking
about what happened 30 years ago?

270
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:21,158
- Why? Did someone say something?
- Yeah.

271
00:18:21,490 --> 00:18:22,947
People always have something to say.

272
00:18:23,010 --> 00:18:26,006
She's always being ostracized.
You don't know, right?

273
00:18:26,341 --> 00:18:27,975
Do you know how unfair that is?

274
00:18:27,978 --> 00:18:31,023
No matter how well she paints
or how well she does in school,

275
00:18:31,069 --> 00:18:33,467
when it really matters,
it's where she comes from.

276
00:18:33,953 --> 00:18:38,896
You cursed her the moment she was born
just because she's my daughter.

277
00:18:40,770 --> 00:18:44,513
I'm okay. I'm the one at fault.

278
00:18:45,608 --> 00:18:50,044
But what did she ever do to deserve this?

279
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:53,515
Why did you make her suffer like this?

280
00:18:56,155 --> 00:18:57,423
Seriously!

281
00:19:40,744 --> 00:19:42,842
Ji Ni, want to grab a drink tonight?

282
00:19:44,248 --> 00:19:45,317
Sure.

283
00:19:46,150 --> 00:19:49,258
- Today was really rough.
- Your mom must've had it hard too.

284
00:19:49,448 --> 00:19:51,327
I'd rather be the one who gets hurt.

285
00:19:52,752 --> 00:19:54,727
I can't stand seeing my mom suffer.

286
00:19:56,029 --> 00:19:59,373
- If only I had never been born...
- Hey! Don't say that.

287
00:20:00,968 --> 00:20:04,225
But do you really think
Do Hee painted the picture she submitted?

288
00:20:04,885 --> 00:20:07,321
I bet that girl had someone else
paint it for her.

289
00:20:07,477 --> 00:20:10,328
You think I don't know Do Hee's work?
She can't even paint.

290
00:20:12,265 --> 00:20:14,008
I don't want to think
about it anymore today.

291
00:20:15,395 --> 00:20:16,502
Yeah. Get some rest.

292
00:20:16,932 --> 00:20:18,727
I'll cheer you up tonight.

293
00:20:20,370 --> 00:20:22,131
- I'm off.
- Okay.

294
00:20:28,698 --> 00:20:30,338
I'll get her medicine ready
and bring it over.

295
00:20:30,341 --> 00:20:33,849
- No, it's okay.
- Don't be silly.

296
00:20:33,852 --> 00:20:35,912
A miscarriage is hard on her body.

297
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:38,031
Are we strangers?

298
00:20:38,472 --> 00:20:42,521
She's your daughter-in-law, so she's
family to me. I should take care of her.

299
00:20:43,833 --> 00:20:46,443
Okay. Then I'll stop by for a bit.

300
00:20:46,446 --> 00:20:49,421
I'll have it ready. See you.

301
00:21:12,676 --> 00:21:14,449
Hey, my beloved nephew.

302
00:21:14,472 --> 00:21:17,000
- How's the preparation going?
- What preparation?

303
00:21:17,867 --> 00:21:19,658
- The proposal?
- Hey, Im Ji Hu!

304
00:21:19,894 --> 00:21:22,030
Uncle, do you have to yell?

305
00:21:22,092 --> 00:21:24,552
How am I supposed not to yell?

306
00:21:24,972 --> 00:21:27,733
I want to get Yeong Ju
out of this family mess...

307
00:21:27,790 --> 00:21:29,831
as soon as possible.

308
00:21:29,892 --> 00:21:32,452
She's still spending all her time
taking care of her kids.

309
00:21:33,469 --> 00:21:34,513
Yeah.

310
00:21:34,570 --> 00:21:37,798
Make it amazing. Make it perfect.

311
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:43,380
You're not even trying.

312
00:21:54,286 --> 00:21:55,931
Why aren't you eating?

313
00:21:57,065 --> 00:21:58,479
I don't like seaweed soup.

314
00:22:00,021 --> 00:22:04,496
You said they eat pork trotter porridge
after giving birth in Vietnam, right?

315
00:22:04,630 --> 00:22:07,245
- Want me to make some?
- You remember?

316
00:22:07,595 --> 00:22:10,542
I think you craved it
after O Reum was born.

317
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:14,127
No. Maybe later.

318
00:22:16,791 --> 00:22:19,017
I'm going to the clinic
to get your medicine.

319
00:22:19,132 --> 00:22:21,680
I'll pick up some pork trotters.
We can make the porridge again.

320
00:22:22,682 --> 00:22:23,682
It's okay.

321
00:22:54,223 --> 00:22:55,646
Seung Hyun.

322
00:22:56,618 --> 00:22:59,821
I saw you working
at the school post office,

323
00:23:00,029 --> 00:23:03,660
I fell for you at first sight
and married you.

324
00:23:03,906 --> 00:23:05,231
Then we had O Reum,

325
00:23:05,729 --> 00:23:07,814
and I was so happy.

326
00:23:16,874 --> 00:23:19,400
You were always there for me.

327
00:23:20,983 --> 00:23:23,873
I wanted to build a warm family with you,

328
00:23:26,803 --> 00:23:28,382
but I think I failed.

329
00:23:47,607 --> 00:23:50,458
I need some time to myself.

330
00:23:52,516 --> 00:23:53,933
Please don't look for me.

331
00:23:58,481 --> 00:23:59,836
I'm sorry...

332
00:24:01,417 --> 00:24:02,483
it came to this.

333
00:24:06,508 --> 00:24:08,991
(I need some time to myself.)

334
00:24:08,993 --> 00:24:11,691
(Please don't look for me.
I'm sorry it came to this.)

335
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:20,881
- Hey.
- Yeah? What is it?

336
00:24:23,543 --> 00:24:25,712
I think I should check your pulse.

337
00:24:25,781 --> 00:24:28,290
- But right now...
- Don't worry.

338
00:24:28,677 --> 00:24:30,980
I'm making a house call
as a doctor of Korean medicine.

339
00:24:32,164 --> 00:24:33,861
- Okay, then.
- Let's go.

340
00:24:34,290 --> 00:24:35,290
Okay.

341
00:24:48,972 --> 00:24:51,437
- Mom.
- Seung Hyun, you're home early.

342
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:52,930
- Hello.
- Where's Mai?

343
00:24:52,985 --> 00:24:55,681
- Mai's home.
- She's not home.

344
00:24:55,996 --> 00:24:58,251
Mom, where did you go,
leaving her here alone?

345
00:24:58,341 --> 00:25:01,187
- What do you mean? I was with him...
- Enough.

346
00:25:03,153 --> 00:25:04,375
Seung Hyun.

347
00:25:08,458 --> 00:25:09,713
Why is he...

348
00:26:04,357 --> 00:26:06,357
(The late Cha O Reum)

349
00:26:07,789 --> 00:26:08,967
O Reum,

350
00:26:10,547 --> 00:26:11,937
I...

351
00:26:13,229 --> 00:26:15,103
won't be able to come for a while.

352
00:26:17,844 --> 00:26:19,208
My O Reum,

353
00:26:21,835 --> 00:26:23,896
I love you so much.

354
00:27:01,793 --> 00:27:04,658
- You couldn't find her?
- Mom,

355
00:27:05,430 --> 00:27:07,246
How did you hold back all this time?

356
00:27:08,193 --> 00:27:09,980
Why did you deny yourself
the chance to be in love?

357
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:12,208
- Seung Hyun.
- Can't you go one day without seeing him?

358
00:27:12,910 --> 00:27:15,423
Can't you just stay by Mai's side
for a while?

359
00:27:15,465 --> 00:27:17,566
I was on my way to bring her medicine
and check her pulse.

360
00:27:17,604 --> 00:27:20,296
- You don't know what you're saying.
- "Check her pulse?"

361
00:27:21,010 --> 00:27:22,753
It's obvious what medicine
she needs after a miscarriage.

362
00:27:23,665 --> 00:27:26,110
And couldn't you have come alone?

363
00:27:26,454 --> 00:27:27,771
Do you have to go everywhere together?

364
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:32,106
You little brat. I'm hurting too.
I'm grieving too.

365
00:27:32,710 --> 00:27:35,873
Did I tell Mai to leave?
What did I even do to you?

366
00:27:35,911 --> 00:27:38,762
If you'd stayed home,
you could've stopped her from leaving.

367
00:27:39,190 --> 00:27:42,210
Did you really have to leave her alone
and go around with that man?

368
00:27:42,248 --> 00:27:43,402
Cha Seung Hyun!

369
00:27:45,035 --> 00:27:48,698
I'm so disappointed in you, Mom.
I'm really hurt.

370
00:28:16,990 --> 00:28:20,008
(Family Register)

371
00:28:20,080 --> 00:28:21,440
You only protect your own family?

372
00:28:21,511 --> 00:28:23,052
That's just selfishness
on your family's part.

373
00:28:23,094 --> 00:28:25,738
- Don't be so quick to cast stones.
- Ji Ni.

374
00:28:25,814 --> 00:28:27,600
You saw Do Hee's painting.

375
00:28:27,642 --> 00:28:29,290
It has zero creativity.

376
00:28:29,330 --> 00:28:30,631
It's just something she learned
at an art academy.

377
00:28:30,677 --> 00:28:32,410
I'll send you the file.
Better than Na Ji Ni's, right?

378
00:28:32,463 --> 00:28:33,991
Then why are you so obsessed
with Na Ji Ni?

379
00:28:34,033 --> 00:28:36,846
I guess you and I played Cupid.

380
00:28:36,909 --> 00:28:38,008
Who said you could break up?

381
00:28:38,050 --> 00:28:39,550
You think you can just end this
whenever you want?

382
00:28:39,604 --> 00:28:41,595
You remember our promise yesterday, right?
The proposal.

383
00:28:42,772 --> 00:28:44,772
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
